   "source": [
    "## 4. Preprocessing\n",
    "\n",
    "We build this section as a set of clear, reusable steps so that the\n",
    "**exact same transformations** can be applied later to new customer\n",
    "data inside the Streamlit app. We'll persist:\n",
    "\n",
    "- The list of **label encoders** (one per categorical column)\n",
    "- The **column/feature order** the model was trained on\n",
    "- Optionally a **scaler** for numeric columns (kept for completeness —\n",
    "  tree-based models don't strictly need scaling, but it's saved so the\n",
    "  pipeline can be swapped for a scale-sensitive model later)\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4.1 Handle `TotalCharges` and drop `customerID`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1e22aa9b",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-01T05:33:13.989600Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-01T05:33:13.989405Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.018123Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.016923Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "data = df.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# TotalCharges has a few rows with blank strings instead of numbers.\n",
    "# Coerce to numeric, then fill missing values with the median.\n",
    "data[\"TotalCharges\"] = pd.to_numeric(data[\"TotalCharges\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "\n",
    "n_missing = data[\"TotalCharges\"].isnull().sum()\n",
    "print(f\"Rows with missing TotalCharges after coercion: {n_missing}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "data[\"TotalCharges\"] = data[\"TotalCharges\"].fillna(data[\"TotalCharges\"].median())\n",
    "\n",
    "# customerID is just an identifier — it carries no predictive signal\n",
    "data.drop(columns=[\"customerID\"], inplace=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "data.head()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "29250159",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.2 Encode the target variable"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f97f6f64",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.020251Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.019999Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.029034Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.027833Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Churn: \"Yes\" -> 1, \"No\" -> 0\n",
    "data[\"Churn\"] = data[\"Churn\"].map({\"Yes\": 1, \"No\": 0})\n",
    "data[\"Churn\"].value_counts()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0f55d2b1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.3 Encode categorical feature columns\n",
    "\n",
    "We use `LabelEncoder` (one per column) rather than one-hot encoding, to\n",
    "keep the feature set compact and match the reusable-encoder pattern\n",
    "used by the web app (each encoder is saved and re-applied to new\n",
    "input rows at inference time)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cb640d4f",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.031993Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.031176Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.057480Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.056351Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Identify categorical (object-type) feature columns, excluding the target\n",
    "categorical_cols = data.select_dtypes(include=\"object\").columns.tolist()\n",
    "print(\"Categorical columns to encode:\", categorical_cols)\n",
    "\n",
    "encoders = {}\n",
    "for col in categorical_cols:\n",
    "    le = LabelEncoder()\n",
    "    data[col] = le.fit_transform(data[col])\n",
    "    encoders[col] = le\n",
    "\n",
    "data.head()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5cd4adb5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.4 Separate features (X) and target (y)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9bb30e1e",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.059711Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.059487Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.067823Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.066674Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X = data.drop(columns=[\"Churn\"])\n",
    "y = data[\"Churn\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "feature_names = X.columns.tolist()\n",
    "print(f\"Number of features: {len(feature_names)}\")\n",
    "print(feature_names)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d40a94fd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.5 Optional scaler\n",
    "\n",
    "Not required for tree-based models, but we fit and save one anyway so\n",
    "the same preprocessing bundle can support a distance/scale-sensitive\n",
    "model (e.g. Logistic Regression, KNN) without re-doing this section."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "de91ee04",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.069824Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.069634Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.082967Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.081909Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "scaler.fit(X)  # fit on the full feature set; only used if a model needs it\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "53678639",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Train/Test Split & Class Imbalance\n",
    "\n",
    "We split **before** applying SMOTE, and only oversample the **training**\n",
    "set — the test set must stay untouched and reflect the real-world class\n",
    "distribution so evaluation metrics are honest."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9c1c08a0",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.084839Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.084653Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.146249Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.145090Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X, y, test_size=0.20, random_state=RANDOM_STATE, stratify=y\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Before SMOTE:\")\n",
    "print(y_train.value_counts())\n",
    "\n",
    "smote = SMOTE(random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n",
    "X_train_res, y_train_res = smote.fit_resample(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nAfter SMOTE (training set only):\")\n",
    "print(y_train_res.value_counts())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "76a4ea6c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Model Training\n",
    "\n",
    "We train three classifiers on the SMOTE-balanced training set:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Decision Tree** — simple, interpretable baseline\n",
    "2. **Random Forest** — bagged ensemble of trees, usually more robust\n",
    "3. **XGBoost** — gradient-boosted trees, typically the strongest performer\n",
    "\n",
    "Cross-validation (5-fold, stratified) is run on the **balanced training\n",
    "data** to get a stable estimate of each model's generalization\n",
    "performance before looking at the held-out test set."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "034c383e",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.148446Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-01T05:33:14.148176Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-01T05:33:16.556821Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-08-01T05:33:16.555514Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "models = {\n",
    "    \"Decision Tree\": DecisionTreeClassifier(random_state=RANDOM_STATE),\n",
    "    \"Random Forest\": RandomForestClassifier(random_state=RANDOM_STATE, n_estimators=200),\n",
    "    \"XGBoost\": XGBClassifier(\n",
    "        random_state=RANDOM_STATE,\n",
    "        eval_metric=\"logloss\",\n",
    "    ),\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "cv = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n",
    "cv_results = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "for name, model in models.items():\n",
    "    scores = cross_val_score(model, X_train_res, y_train_res, cv=cv, scoring=\"accuracy\")\n",
    "    cv_results[name] = scores\n",
    "    print(f\"{name}: mean CV accuracy = {scores.mean():.4f} (+/- {scores.std():.4f})\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d713a592",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-08-01T05:33:16.558720Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-08-01T05:33:16.558511Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-08-01T05:33:17.023373Z",
